Interfaces between the emulated hardware and the host. Headers here must not
include operating system headers; the implementations live in the sibling
directories and are chosen by the build.

Threads: the processors, the event loop and the window system each run on a
thread of their own, and all of them reach the devices through one device
lock (src/core/device_lock.h).

- Every method of a host object here is called with the device lock held,
  and possibly from any of those threads.
- A host object calls a device (a target, a completion, a screen source)
  only with the device lock held; a thread of its own takes the lock first.
- A host object that must do work on a thread of its own, such as a window,
  hands it over rather than doing it in the call.
